serves 2

marinade:
1 lb flank steak (sliced thin against the grain)
2 tsp netural oil
2 tsp shaozing wine or dry cooking sherry
1 tsp soy sauce
2 tsp arrowroot or 1 Tbsp corn starch
1 Tbsp water
1/4 tsp baking soda

sauce:
1/4 cup light brown sugar
3/4 cup hot water
1/4 cup soy sauce or tamari
1 tsp dark soy sauce (optional)

for coating and searing:
1/3 cup arrowroot, or 1/2 cup cornstarch
2/3 cup neutral oil

remainder:
1 tsp ginger (minced)
8 dried red chili peppers
3 cloves garlic
4 scallions
1 Tbsp arrowroot, mixed with 2 Tbsp water


Combine the beef with the marinade and marinade
for at least 1 hour.  If too dry, add 1 Tbsp water

Mix the sauce; dissolve the sugar in the water and then
add the soy sauce/tamari

Dredge the marinated beef slices in the
cornstarch

Sear the meat in oil at high heat for 1 minute
on each side, then transfer to a plate.

Retaining 1 Tbsp, drain the oil from the wok
At medium high, cook the ginger and chili
peppers for 15 seconds, then add the garlic
and white part of scallions.  Stir for 15 seconds,
then add the sauce.  Simmer for 2 minutes and slowly
add the arrowroot slurry.  Cook until the sauce
has thickened

Add the beef and remainder of scallions, toss
for about 30 seconds.

Serve over rice
